<title>USA: Fluor Corp Q2 net loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Fluor Corp Q2 net loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q2 ended April 30			  1997		   1996</p>
<p> Revenues				 $ 3,185.8	   $ 2,582.2</p>
<p>Costs and Expenses</p>
<p>    Cost of Revenues		    3,259.6	     2,477.2</p>
<p>    Corporate G&amp;A			     3.2		  11.3</p>
<p>    Net Interest				1.4		 (3.4)</p>
<p> Total Costs and Expenses	     3,264.2	     2,485.1</p>
<p> Earnings (Loss) before Income Taxes  (78.4)		 97.1</p>
<p> Income Tax (Benefit) Expense	   (8.3)		  33.4</p>
<p> Net Earnings (Loss)		     (70.1)		  63.7</p>
<p> Net Earnings (Loss) per Share	 (0.83)		  0.75</p>
<p>SIX MONTHS</p>
<p> Revenues				   6,619.9	     4,984.6</p>
<p>Costs and Expenses</p>
<p>  Cost of Revenues			6,586.9	     4,780.5</p>
<p>  Corporate G&amp;A				14.1		  24.6</p>
<p>  Net Interest				  1.7		 (7.3)</p>
<p> Total Costs and Expenses	     6,602.7	     4,797.8</p>
<p> Earnings before Income Taxes	    17.2		 186.8</p>
<p> Income Tax Expense			  25.3		  65.7</p>
<p> Net Earnings (Loss)			(8.1)		 121.1</p>
<p> Net Earnings (Loss) per Share	 (0.10)		  1.43</p>
<p>(in millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTES: Company said its Fluor Daniel unit had Q2 operating loss $110 million. Loss included provision of $120 million for project overruns and a $20 million charge for implementation of cost reduction program.</p>
<p>For six months, Fluor Daniel showed operating loss of $36 million vs profit $147 million a year ago.</p>
<p>New engineering and construction awards in Q2 were $3.2 billion versus $3 billion a year ago. Backlog rose 5 percent to $16.1 billion from $15.4 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>Fluor's A.T. Massey unit increased operating profits 15 percent to $37 million in Q2 vs a year ago. Unit's six months profits rose 17 percent.</p>
